    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0125" n="21" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg21"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">130 Baird, Annie</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain (Mellon) to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 519</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-11-29">November 29,
                        1932</date>.<lb/>[Received December 7.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s instruction No. 232 of September 26, 1932, File No. 130–Baird,
                    Annie, and to transmit herewith a copy of the note which on October 10 was
                    addressed to the Foreign Office<anchor n="21" xml:id="d17-f1"/> and a copy of
                    the latter’s reply under date of November 28, from which it will be seen that
                    the British authorities are not disposed to certify to the legality of Miss
                    Baird’s adoption. The Embassy has informed the Consul at Dundee in this sense
                    and has added that it was asking the Department to instruct it as to whether
                    Miss Baird is still to be regarded as an American citizen. Instructions in that
                    relation are accordingly respectfully requested.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ray Atherton</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Counselor of Embassy</hi>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d17-a1.xml" xpointer="d17-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
